nstructor invocation (#135287)","ai_tool":"Copilot"},{"repo_name":"sgl-project/sglang","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:43:50Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"b9f5d7000c0f69a67c497c363555f9977f053cb0","github_link":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/commit/b9f5d7000c0f69a67c497c363555f9977f053cb0","commit_subject":"[Fix] disaggregation: Bind NIXL transfer workers to the rank's device (#47255)","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"vpnhood/VpnHood","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:43:39Z","branch":"develop","commit_sha":"b3c8133b6727af8ac38f090b44da2742744678cb","github_link":"https://github.com/vpnhood/VpnHood/commit/b3c8133b6727af8ac38f090b44da2742744678cb","commit_subject":"Storage: its two design decisions as comments where they govern. IStorageProvider stays sync: it holds the app's own state, which the app reads as it starts, on the main thread from each head's sync entry, and writes behind sync setters; a store on the network would need a contract of its own, async, with a local copy and timeouts. Storage is one class over a provider of full paths, not storages that wrap their parents: a wrapper hands its parent a path, so every level would take paths and check them. Comments only.","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"vpnhood/VpnHood","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:43:38Z","branch":"develop","commit_sha":"e8a1bca23f4473b22d12ee662a6979d246bb47d3","github_link":"https://github.com/vpnhood/VpnHood/commit/e8a1bca23f4473b22d12ee662a6979d246bb47d3","commit_subject":"App storage on an Apple TV: a deletion that fails frees nothing of the budget. KeyValueStorageProvider.Delete took the entry off its count before removing it, so a removal the store failed left the entry in the defaults but out of the count, and later writes could take the defaults past the budget. It now keeps the new count only once the entry is gone, as Write does. Checked: TvStorageTest's new failed deletion, which failed before the change, and the rest of TvStorageTest.","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"rep